{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-85716","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120314","text":"SpecPrompt — Implementation Build Prompt"}]},{"id":"blk-85717","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120315","marks":["bold"],"text":"Version:"},{"id":"spn-120316","text":" 1.0 | "},{"id":"spn-120317","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-120318","text":" April 2026 | "},{"id":"spn-120319","marks":["bold"],"text":"Type:"},{"id":"spn-120320","text":" Full Implementation (CLI + MCP + Supabase)"}]},{"id":"blk-85718","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120321","text":"Your Mission"}]},{"id":"blk-85719","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120322","text":"You are building "},{"id":"spn-120323","marks":["bold"],"text":"SpecPrompt"},{"id":"spn-120324","text":" — the standards layer of the [&] Protocol dark factory pipeline. SpecPrompt defines the SPEC.md format (machine-parseable agent specifications) and provides the CLI toolchain, MCP server, and Supabase registry that make specs the entry point for autonomous code generation."}]},{"id":"blk-85720","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120325","marks":["bold"],"text":"Read `docs/spec/README.md` fully before writing a single line."},{"id":"spn-120326","text":" It is the authoritative spec."}]},{"id":"blk-85721","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120327","text":"SpecPrompt is the "},{"id":"spn-120328","marks":["bold"],"text":"first stage"},{"id":"spn-120329","text":" of the dark factory pipeline:"}]},{"id":"blk-85722","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SpecPrompt (spec in) → Agentelic (build) → OS-008 (enforce) → FleetPrompt (distribute) → RuneFort (observe)"},{"id":"blk-85723","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120330","text":"Target Stack"}]},{"id":"blk-85724","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Language:   Elixir 1.17+ / OTP 27\nCLI:        Mix escript (specprompt validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff, publish)\nMCP:        JSON-RPC over HTTP (spec_validate, spec_lint, spec_generate, spec_test_gen,\n            spec_test_compile, spec_test_approve, spec_diff, spec_search)\nDatabase:   PostgreSQL via shared Supabase (spec.* schema, migration range TBD)\nAuth:       Supabase Auth (shared [&] ecosystem — amp.profiles, amp.workspaces)\nParser:     PEG grammar (see spec section 4.4) — implement in both Elixir and TypeScript\nTesting:    ExUnit (Elixir), Vitest (TypeScript parser)\nDeploy:     Fly.io (MCP server) + npm (TypeScript parser)"},{"id":"blk-85725","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120331","text":"Dual-Mode Architecture"}]},{"id":"blk-85726","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120332","text":"SpecPrompt operates in two modes. Both must work from day one:"}]},{"id":"blk-85727","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120333","text":"Filesystem Mode (default, zero-cost)"}]},{"id":"blk-85728","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85730","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120334","text":"CLI reads "},{"id":"spn-120335","marks":["code"],"text":".md"},{"id":"spn-120336","text":" files from local git repos"}]}],"id":"blk-85729","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85732","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120337","text":"No auth, no database, no network"}]}],"id":"blk-85731","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85734","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120338","text":"All tools work offline: validate, lint, test-gen, test-compile, diff"}]}],"id":"blk-85733","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85736","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120339","text":"Audit via git history"}]}],"id":"blk-85735","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85738","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120340","text":"This is the \"PULSE scales down\" demonstration"}]}],"id":"blk-85737","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-85739","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120341","text":"Registry Mode (multi-tenant dark factory)"}]},{"id":"blk-85740","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85742","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120342","text":"Specs stored in Supabase "},{"id":"spn-120343","marks":["code"],"text":"spec.specs"},{"id":"spn-120344","text":" table"}]}],"id":"blk-85741","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85744","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120345","text":"Workspace-scoped via "},{"id":"spn-120346","marks":["code"],"text":"amp.workspaces"}]}],"id":"blk-85743","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85746","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120347","text":"Auth via Supabase Auth (same identity as all [&] products)"}]}],"id":"blk-85745","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85748","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120348","text":"Visibility: private | workspace | public"}]}],"id":"blk-85747","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85750","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120349","text":"Pipeline triggers via Supabase Realtime or CloudEvents webhooks"}]}],"id":"blk-85749","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85752","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120350","text":"Required for dark factory automation"}]}],"id":"blk-85751","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-85753","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120351","text":"Repository Structure"}]},{"id":"blk-85754","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120352","text":"Create this structure inside "},{"id":"spn-120353","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt.com/"},{"id":"spn-120354","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-85755","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"specprompt.com/\n├── lib/\n│   ├── specprompt/\n│   │   ├── parser.ex              # PEG-based SPEC.md parser (section 4.3-4.4)\n│   │   ├── spec.ex                # SpecPrompt.Spec Ecto schema (section 4.6)\n│   │   ├── capability.ex          # SpecPrompt.Capability embedded schema\n│   │   ├── constraint.ex          # SpecPrompt.Constraint embedded schema\n│   │   ├── acceptance_test.ex     # SpecPrompt.AcceptanceTest embedded schema\n│   │   ├── compiled_test.ex       # SpecPrompt.CompiledTest embedded schema (NEW)\n│   │   ├── dependency.ex          # SpecPrompt.Dependency embedded schema\n│   │   ├── changelog_entry.ex     # SpecPrompt.ChangelogEntry embedded schema\n│   │   ├── validator.ex           # Validation rules (section 4.7 — all MUST + SHOULD rules)\n│   │   ├── linter.ex              # Best-practice linting\n│   │   ├── differ.ex              # Spec version diffing\n│   │   ├── test_generator.ex      # Generate test scaffolding from acceptance tests\n│   │   ├── test_compiler.ex       # Compile natural language tests → Agentelic DSL assertions (NEW)\n│   │   ├── publisher.ex           # Publish to FleetPrompt registry or Supabase\n│   │   ├── registry.ex            # Supabase registry client (spec.specs CRUD)\n│   │   ├── interop/\n│   │   │   ├── ampersand.ex       # Bidirectional ampersand.json mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   │   └── adl.ex             # Bidirectional ADL mapping (section 4.8)\n│   │   └── mcp/\n│   │       ├── server.ex          # MCP JSON-RPC server (section 4.2)\n│   │       └── tools.ex           # Tool definitions and handlers\n│   ├── specprompt.ex              # Application entry point\n│   └── cli.ex                     # CLI escript entry point\n├── test/\n│   ├── parser_test.exs\n│   ├── validator_test.exs\n│   ├── linter_test.exs\n│   ├── test_compiler_test.exs\n│   ├── differ_test.exs\n│   └── fixtures/\n│       ├── valid_spec.md          # Use the customer-support example from spec section 3.3\n│       ├── invalid_spec.md        # Missing required sections\n│       └── compiled_tests.json    # Pre-compiled test assertions\n├── npm/                           # TypeScript parser package (@specprompt/parser)\n│   ├── src/\n│   │   ├── parser.ts\n│   │   ├── types.ts\n│   │   └── index.ts\n│   ├── test/\n│   │   └── parser.test.ts\n│   ├── package.json\n│   └── tsconfig.json\n├── mix.exs\n├── Dockerfile\n└── fly.toml"},{"id":"blk-85756","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120355","text":"Implementation Order"}]},{"id":"blk-85757","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120356","text":"Phase 1: Parser + Validator (week 1)"}]},{"id":"blk-85758","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85760","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120357","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement PEG parser"},{"id":"spn-120358","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-120359","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/parser.ex"},{"id":"spn-120360","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-85759","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-85761","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85763","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120361","text":"Parse YAML frontmatter (all fields from spec section 4.5, including new "},{"id":"spn-120362","marks":["code"],"text":"workspace_id"},{"id":"spn-120363","text":", "},{"id":"spn-120364","marks":["code"],"text":"visibility"},{"id":"spn-120365","text":", "},{"id":"spn-120366","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-120367","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-85762","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85765","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120368","text":"Parse H2 sections: Purpose, Capabilities, Constraints, Acceptance Tests, Architecture, Dependencies, Changelog"}]}],"id":"blk-85764","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85767","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120369","text":"Extract structured data into "},{"id":"spn-120370","marks":["code"],"text":"SpecPrompt.Spec"},{"id":"spn-120371","text":" schema"}]}],"id":"blk-85766","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85769","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120372","text":"Compute "},{"id":"spn-120373","marks":["code"],"text":"source_hash"},{"id":"spn-120374","text":" (SHA-256 of raw SPEC.md content)"}]}],"id":"blk-85768","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85771","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120375","text":"Return "},{"id":"spn-120376","marks":["code"],"text":"{:ok, %SpecPrompt.Spec{}}"},{"id":"spn-120377","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-120378","marks":["code"],"text":"{:error, [errors]}"}]}],"id":"blk-85770","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-85772","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85774","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120379","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement validator"},{"id":"spn-120380","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-120381","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/validator.ex"},{"id":"spn-120382","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-85773","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-85775","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85777","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120383","text":"All 8 MUST rules from spec section 4.7"}]}],"id":"blk-85776","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85779","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120384","text":"All 7 SHOULD warnings (including 3 new compiled test warnings)"}]}],"id":"blk-85778","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120385","text":"Return structured validation result with line numbers"}]}],"id":"blk-85780","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-85782","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85784","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120386","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement CLI"},{"id":"spn-120387","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-120388","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/cli.ex"},{"id":"spn-120389","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-85783","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-85785","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85787","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120390","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt validate SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-120391","text":" — parse + validate, exit 0/1"}]}],"id":"blk-85786","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85789","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120392","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt lint SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-120393","text":" — validate + SHOULD warnings"}]}],"id":"blk-85788","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-85790","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85792","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120394","marks":["bold"],"text":"Write tests"},{"id":"spn-120395","text":" against the customer-support example from spec section 3.3"}]}],"id":"blk-85791","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-85793","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-120396","text":"Phase 2: Test Compilation (week 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-85794","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120397","text":"This is the critical dark factory bridge — turning natural language acceptance tests into executable assertions."}]},{"id":"blk-85795","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85797","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120398","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement test compiler"},{"id":"spn-120399","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-120400","marks":["code"],"text":"lib/specprompt/test_compiler.ex"},{"id":"spn-120401","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-85796","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-85798","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85800","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120402","text":"Input: "},{"id":"spn-120403","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.Spec{}"},{"id":"spn-120404","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-120405","marks":["code"],"text":"acceptance_tests"}]}],"id":"blk-85799","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85802","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120406","text":"For each acceptance test, generate a "},{"id":"spn-120407","marks":["code"],"text":"%SpecPrompt.CompiledTest{}"},{"id":"spn-120408","text":":"}]}],"id":"blk-85801","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85804","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120409","marks":["code"],"text":"setup"},{"id":"spn-120410","text":": mocked tool states derived from the "},{"id":"spn-120411","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-120412","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-85803","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85806","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120413","marks":["code"],"text":"input"},{"id":"spn-120414","text":": agent input derived from the "},{"id":"spn-120415","marks":["code"],"text":"given"},{"id":"spn-120416","text":" clause"}]}],"id":"blk-85805","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85808","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120417","marks":["code"],"text":"assertions"},{"id":"spn-120418","text":": list of Agentelic DSL assertions:"}]}],"id":"blk-85807","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85810","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120419","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :contains, value: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-120420","text":" — expected text in output"}]}],"id":"blk-85809","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85812","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120421","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_called, tool: \"...\", args: %{}}"},{"id":"spn-120422","text":" — expected tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-85811","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85814","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120423","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :tool_not_called, tool: \"...\"}"},{"id":"spn-120424","text":" — forbidden tool invocation"}]}],"id":"blk-85813","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85816","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120425","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :escalated, value: true/false}"},{"id":"spn-120426","text":" — escalation check"}]}],"id":"blk-85815","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85818","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120427","marks":["code"],"text":"%{type: :constraint_respected, constraint_index: N}"},{"id":"spn-120428","text":" — constraint enforcement"}]}],"id":"blk-85817","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85820","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120429","text":"Compilation is "},{"id":"spn-120430","marks":["bold"],"text":"LLM-assisted on first pass"},{"id":"spn-120431","text":": send the spec + acceptance test to an LLM, ask it to generate the assertion mapping"}]}],"id":"blk-85819","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85822","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120432","text":"Cache compiled tests by "},{"id":"spn-120433","marks":["code"],"text":"{source_hash, test_index}"},{"id":"spn-120434","text":" — unchanged tests reuse prior compilations"}]}],"id":"blk-85821","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85824","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120435","text":"Mark all compiled tests as "},{"id":"spn-120436","marks":["code"],"text":"approved: false"},{"id":"spn-120437","text":" initially"}]}],"id":"blk-85823","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-85825","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85827","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120438","marks":["bold"],"text":"Implement approval workflow"}]}],"id":"blk-85826","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-85828","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85830","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120439","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --output tests/compiled.json"},{"id":"spn-120440","text":" — compile all tests"}]}],"id":"blk-85829","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85832","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120441","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --approve"},{"id":"spn-120442","text":" — mark all compiled tests as approved"}]}],"id":"blk-85831","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85834","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120443","marks":["code"],"text":"specprompt test-compile SPEC.md --status"},{"id":"spn-120444","text":" — show compilation + approval status"}]}],"id":"blk-85833","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85836","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120445","text":"Only approved tests are used by Agentelic in the dark factory pipeline"}]}],"id":"blk-85835","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-85837","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-85839","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-120446","marks":["bold"],"text":"Important constraint"},{"id":"spn-120447","text":": The test compiler itself does NOT call LLMs. It generates a structured prompt that an external LLM (via Agente